  "Question": "The sum of the first eighty positive odd integers subtracted from the sum of the first eighty positive even integers is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0\\)",
    "B": "\\(20\\)",
    "C": "\\(40\\)",
    "D": "\\(60\\)",
    "E": "\\(80\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Each positive even integer is one greater than the corresponding positive odd integer. Subtracting the odd sum from the even sum and grouping corresponding terms gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&(2+4+\\cdots+160)-(1+3+\\cdots+159)\\\\\n&\\qquad=(2-1)+(4-3)+\\cdots+(160-159).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nEvery term from each sum appears in exactly one of these \\(80\\) pairs, and each pair equals \\(1\\). The difference is therefore \\(80\\cdot1=\\boxed{80}\\), choice E.",
